Your HP aren't that low. If you quaff all your potions immediately after
entering the dungeon (I keep one normal healing potion for emergencies),
you've got 23-26 HP to start with. Add that to the wand of sleep you start
with, and you're pretty safe.

> I'd really like to hear from some protection-racketeers about what
> their strategies (and success rates) are *after* they've bought
> protection. What do they do next? At what point do they decide to
> start levelling up? Do they really end up getting much further in the
> dungeon than they would have if they hadn't used that strategy?

After I've bought protection, I usually go back up to pick up all the yet
unidentified armour that I had to leave behind not to become burdened, to
BUC-id it and try it on. After I've cleard the upper levels of the mines
and the dungeon, I'm usually AC -15 or somesuch. While exploring upwards
(there might also be unmapped parts of the mines, if I found the stairs
quickly going down), I usually gain XP quite fast, and get to level 5 or
6. Then, I do Sokoban for the rings, wands, food and prize, and go back to
Town to BUC-id the newly found items. Then I go for the luckstone (I'm
usually level 8 ot 9 by then).

